# Design system first

UI in this repo comes from **`@elirobinson/react`** (components, hooks), **`@elirobinson/tokens`** (color, type, space, radius, shadow, motion), and **`@elirobinson/ai-patterns`** (UI contracts and working patterns). No other component library. No hardcoded design values.

Upstream: https://github.com/EliRobinson/design-system

## Discover before you build

Never rely on a remembered or documented component list — it goes stale on every design system release. Ask the installed packages:

```bash
pnpm ds                  # components (+ exports & variants), hooks, typography classes, token groups
pnpm ds props <Name>     # props and variant unions; accepts `Card` or `molecules/Card`
pnpm ds tokens [filter]  # tokens and values
pnpm ds classes [filter] # CSS classes the design system ships
pnpm ds contracts        # machine-checkable UI rules you must satisfy
pnpm ds patterns         # working principles, including the definition of done
pnpm ds prompts [name]   # prompt templates
```

`pnpm exec elirobinson-ds` is the same command if the `ds` script is not wired up. Deeper detail: `node_modules/@elirobinson/react/src/components/`, `node_modules/@elirobinson/tokens/src/tokens.css`, `node_modules/@elirobinson/react/dist/manifest.json`.

## Rules

- Import per component, full subpath — `pnpm ds props <Name>` prints the exact line. There is no barrel export and a bare package import does not resolve.
- Satisfy `pnpm ds contracts`. Each constraint carries its own `check` and a `verifiedBy` naming what enforces it.
- Use each component's `variant` / `size` props rather than overriding its look with utilities.
- Utility classes are for layout (grid, flex, spacing); the design system owns appearance.
- Colors, radii, shadows, durations, font sizes come from tokens — via mapped utilities, `.t-*` typography classes, or `var(--token)` in arbitrary values. Never a literal.
- With Tailwind v4, `@import '@elirobinson/tokens/tailwind.css'` is what makes `bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border` and friends resolve to tokens.
- Dark mode is `[data-theme="dark"]` (`.dark` also works). With `next-themes`, set `attribute="data-theme"`.
- Token overrides go in an **unlayered** `:root` block — `tokens.css` is unlayered, so an override inside `@layer base` silently loses to it. With `next/font`, re-point the families through `--ds-font-sans-override` / `--ds-font-mono-override` instead, with the font class on `<html>`.
- Stylesheets are imported once in the app shell; don't re-import per component.
- Heroes, page headers, empty states, sidebars are compositions of primitives, not missing components.

## UI copy

Functional copy — errors, empty states, helper and hint text, toasts, labels, button text, tooltips, confirmations, validation — is chrome. State the fact, then the consequence, then the action, and stop.

- No unverifiable frequency claims ("almost always", "this rarely happens").
- No blame attribution ("on their side", "check your connection").
- No filler pacing ("in a moment", "hang tight").
- No unprompted reassurance or apology ("don't worry", "we'll sort it out"). Reassurance only where it answers a question the reader is actually asking, and only as a fact: "You have not been charged."
- No escalation paths nobody asked for; no enthusiasm or exclamation marks.
- Past two short sentences, it is explaining, reassuring, or selling — cut it back.

**Chrome only — not this product's editorial voice.** Marketing prose, conversational surfaces, and written deliverables are content, their voice is deliberate, and this rule does not touch them. Where a surface mixes the two, the chrome follows this rule and the content is left alone.

`@elirobinson/eslint-config` reports the literal phrases, scoped to copy props and chrome components; it never reads ordinary prose. It ships at `warn` so an upgrade cannot fail a build — raise it to `error` once your copy is clean: `designSystem({ copy: { severity: 'error' } })`.

## Missing something?

1. Compose from existing primitives.
2. Pull in the repo's sanctioned gap-filler and restyle it with tokens.
3. Hand-roll from tokens as a last resort, and flag it as a design system gap worth upstreaming.

MUI, Chakra, Ant Design, Mantine, HeroUI, Headless UI, DaisyUI, direct Radix imports, and bare `@elirobinson/*` imports are blocked by `@elirobinson/eslint-config`. Don't work around it.

## Done

Run `pnpm ds patterns` and work the **Definition of Done for UI work** checklist. It lives in the package so it can't go stale here.
